cycles 4971 shown 00011bff9d
the checks:
the line carries C0DE+BEEF= (10 characters of 10 bits)
the board's UART received C0DE+BEEF=
Hex1000.xtl replayed 4971 clocks from the circuit's K: A, S, PC and PA agree at every one
the display ends showing 17FCD, the evaluator's (hx:c_alc)
the cue sheet:
[[cue]]
n = 1
start = 0.000
end = 3.200
caption = "HEX1000: C0DE+BEEF= typed at a 4-bit machine, its circuit simulated clock by clock"

[[cue]]
n = 2
start = 3.800
end = 10.000
caption = "slow motion: each key arrives on the serial line as 10 bits, a start bit, 8 data bits from the lowest, a stop bit"

[[cue]]
n = 3
start = 10.800
end = 16.200
caption = "the board queues it; the machine selects the key columns one by one (R8 to R13) and finds its row on K"

[[cue]]
n = 4
start = 17.800
end = 24.800
caption = "time-lapse: the other 9 keys wait in the queue, a few hundred clocks each, and the display shows them"

[[cue]]
n = 5
start = 25.800
end = 35.200
caption = "slow motion: the sum, a digit at a time with its carry (AMAAC), the RAM's bars changing"

[[cue]]
n = 6
start = 36.800
end = 42.000
caption = "17FCD after 3044 clocks: the circuit's display, the evaluator's and the browser's agree"


